==Trivia==
* T-Rex has been nominated to be added to the game since [[Updates/7|Update 7]].
* T-Rex has the same price as [[Mammoth]], both costing {{Money|2,700,000}} or {{Robux|2,350}}. However, its trading value is a little higher.
** This also makes T-Rex one of the only fruits that share a monetary value with another fruit, with the second being  [[Tiger]] and [[Yeti]].
* T-Rex is one of the few fruits to leave effects on nearby users' screens when using a move/[[Transformations|transformation]].
* T-Rex's Prey mark does not deal damage to transformed [[Dragon]] users.
* The player has a tail while they have T-Rex equipped. This is only cosmetic and does not add anything, unlike [[Kitsune]]'s Tails.
** This also adds to the fact that T-Rex is one of the only [[Beast]] [[fruits]] to add cosmetics to the user, alongside [[Eagle]].
* Due to the infliction of tick damage on enemies during the [[transformation]], T-Rex can excel in PvP, being able to damage the enemy even at exceedingly high distances. It can also let the user see where the opponent is, making it very hard for them to escape.
** The Prey Mark's tick damage works best when inflicting damage and then getting teleported to [[Portal]]'s {{Ability|Portal|V}}.
** This also works surprisingly well with Portal's {{Ability|Portal|C}}.
* T-Rex, along with [[Dragon]], [[Gas]] and [[Magnet]], are the only unawakenable [[Blox Fruits]] that have unique transformation names ({{Ability|V}} for T-Rex, {{Ability|Dragon|V}} for Dragon, {{Ability|Gas|V}} for Gas, and, '''[V] Maximum Overdrive''' for Magnet) 
* T-Rex, [[Venom]] and [[Dragon]] are the only fruits with a [[Power Meter|Fury Meter]].
* If the opponent stays at the edge of T-Rex's {{Ability|X}} move, they could walk out of it as they are not fully stunned. 
* The in-game T-Rex's design bears resemblance to transformed [[Dragon]]'s western variant, due to the curved, backwards facing horns on both their heads. Their relation is further implied by the fact that both T-Rex and Dragon are linked to the [[Prehistoric Island]]. 
* T-Rex's {{Ability|C}} can be used like [[Flash Step]] if the wall the user is trying to go through is thin enough.
* Strangely,, while using shift lock, the {{Ability|Z}} move glitches sometimes and does not hit the opponent even while well within range. This happens more often if the user is transformed.
* The silhouette of its beast form can be seen when using {{Ability|C}} untransformed.
* T-Rex’s M1’s can hit [[Sea Beast]]s.
* If the user uses Transformed {{Ability|F}} while in water, the player moves to the new area without the jumping animation (More often when using shiftlock). 
* T-Rex is used by the [[Ancient Beast]], and is able to transform into a t-rex nearly twice as big as normal.
* Inside [[Control]]'s domain, this fruit's VFX color turns into a teal color, very similar to the one seen in T-Rex's physical fruit model. 
* Using {{Ability|F}} can let the user go through walls and ceilings. 
* While transformed, the user has no double jump animation.
* There is a very strange glitch with T-Rex that causes players to be flung out of reality and back after using [[Flash Step]] sometimes, and it can cause the user to become very slow, have delayed inputs, unable to air jump or use Flash Step, and lets them move during skills. But worry not, because this glitch can easily be fixed by untransforming.
* Using shiftlock during {{Ability|F}} and turning around can slightly change the trajectory.
* T-Rex is considered to be [[Mammoth]]’s rival.
* T-Rex is one of the fruits most commonly used by scripters due to its fast M1s. Other fruits with similar M1s are [[Kitsune]] and [[Dragon]].
* T-Rex is the only fruit with a M1 in the game that does not give a suspicious kill.
* Pairing T-Rex Prey Mark tick damage with Cyborg V4’s Aftershock tick damage can result in a tick damage stack which is really helpful in PvP to catch runners and dealing with teamers.
* While transforming to the T-rex form while quickly swapping to [[Smoke]], the player will be invisible. However it does not mean that the user is fully undetectable; they are still able be seen with [[Instinct]].
